  "homeGreetingVigil": "night vigil",
  "@homeGreetingVigil": {
    "description": "00:00–04:59. Transcribed: `redesign.html:926` — `vigil:[\"night vigil\",\"سهر الليل\"]`, the fourth arm of the prototype's `hourKey()` (`:983-984`, which returns `vigil` for every hour before five).\n\n**A fourth key where the three before it were this client's decision.** The redesign's own clock has four buckets, and the last one is not the prototype's English `evening` word but a different word with a different meaning — so the boundaries are now the prototype's and `greeting_period.dart` says so."
  },
  "homePeace": "peace",
  "@homePeace": {
    "description": "The greeting's second line, `redesign.html:993` — `el('hiName').textContent = lang==='ar' ? 'سلم، مريم' : 'peace, Mariam'`.\n\n**Half of the prototype's string, deliberately.** `hiName` is one literal with the reader's name inside it, and a name is not translatable — it is `AuthSession.displayName`. So the word and the comma live in this table and the page composes `homePeace` + `homeGreetingSeparator` + the name, which reproduces the prototype's sentence exactly on both arms. The Arabic is the prototype's own two-letter word for peace, not the four-letter greeting of a letter."
  },
  "homeDays": "days",
  "@homeDays": {
    "description": "The unit painted beside the streak number. Transcribed: `redesign.html:925` — `days:[\"days\",\"أيام\"]`, written into the chip's `.sl` span at `:516`.\n\n**Separate from `homeStreakLabel`, which is the announcement's prefix** and a plural noun in Arabic; see that key's description for why it stays a prefix rather than becoming a phrase."
  },
  "homeVerseOfTheDay": "verse of the day",
  "@homeVerseOfTheDay": {
    "description": "The day's card eyebrow, and the card's accessible name. Transcribed: `redesign.html:927` — `votd:[\"verse of the day\",\"آية اليوم\"]`, written into `#votdCard` at `:521`.\n\n**It replaces `homeTodayReading`** (“Today's reading”), which described the panel this card replaces and named no string the redesign draws."
  },
  "homeLastLight": "last light",
  "@homeLastLight": {
    "description": "The last-light card's eyebrow, and the card's accessible name. Transcribed: `redesign.html:928` — `lastW:[\"last light\",\"آخر نور\"]`, written into `#lastCard` at `:525`."
  },
  "homeNoLightRef": "—",
  "@homeNoLightRef": {
    "description": "The reference the same card shows when there is no light: an em dash. Transcribed: `redesign.html:1193` — `el('lastRef').textContent = '—'`.\n\n**The one key in this table whose two values are identical**, and the reason is that it is punctuation: no translation of a dash exists, and an Arabic-specific dash would be a reader-facing change nobody asked for. It replaced `homeWordmark` in `app_localizations_test.dart`'s `mustBeIdentical` set, so the “every other key must differ” rule still has a live exception rather than an empty list."
  },
  "homeNoLight": "no light received yet — open a book below",
  "@homeNoLight": {
    "description": "The last-light card's body when `GET /streak`'s `history` is empty. Transcribed: `redesign.html:929` — `noLight:[...]`, set by `updateLastWidget` at `:1194`.\n\nThe state is real: `history` is the cohort's last thirty scheduled readings (`streak.service.ts:88-96`) and a cohort with none has a reader who has not opened a book. The sentence points at the carousel below it instead of apologising, which is the prototype's own choice and the reason the Arabic names the books rather than the failure."
  },
  "homeResumeHint": "resume where the light left you ›",
  "@homeResumeHint": {
    "description": "The last-light card's hint, shown only when there is a light to resume from. Transcribed: `redesign.html:928` — `resumeHint:[...]`, hidden by `updateLastWidget` when `lastRead` is null (`:1195`).\n\n**The `›` is part of the string and not a drawn glyph.** The prototype writes it into the text (`:528`), so it travels with the sentence and uppercases under LTR with the rest of the `.mono` run; a separate `Icon` would sit outside the run and stay lowercase beside an uppercase sentence."
  },
  "homeSelah": "Selah",
  "@homeSelah": {
    "description": "The selah card's title. Transcribed: `redesign.html:970` — `selah:[\"Selah\",\"سِلاه\"]`.\n\n**The Arabic keeps its tashkeel** (`سِلاه`, a kasra under the seen), because the prototype's own Arabic carries it and a bare `سلاه` is a different spelling of the word. The English is Latin on the Arabic arm's screen too, which is the prototype's arrangement and not an oversight here."
  },
  "homeSecondsOfSilence": "seconds of silence",
  "@homeSecondsOfSilence": {
    "description": "The selah card's second line, **without the number**. Transcribed: `redesign.html:970` — `secs:[\"seconds of silence\",\"ثانية من الصمت\"]`.\n\nThe prototype composes it: `el('selahSub').textContent = \\`${N(selahDur)} ${tr('secs')}\\`` (`:990`). Composing here rather than through a `{seconds}` placeholder is what keeps the Arabic value free of the ASCII placeholder name — `app_localizations_test.dart` fails any non-plural Arabic value holding Latin script, and see `readingCaptionFor`'s description for why the plural keys are the only ones exempt."
  },
  "homeTheLibrary": "the library",
  "@homeTheLibrary": {
    "description": "The carousel's left-hand label. Transcribed: `redesign.html:930` — `lib:[\"the library\",\"المكتبة\"]`, written into `.car-label` at `:535`."
  },
  "homeScrolls": "scrolls",
  "@homeScrolls": {
    "description": "The carousel's first count's unit. Transcribed from `redesign.html:930`'s `libCount` — `\"6 scrolls · 4 open\"`.\n\n**Split in two because the prototype's string has the numbers baked into it and this client's do not.** The catalogue is `LibraryCatalogueRepository.books()` and its length is not a constant, so a single key would have needed an ARB placeholder; a non-plural key with a placeholder puts the ASCII placeholder name in the Arabic value. The page composes `{digits} {homeScrolls} · {digits} {homeOpenBooks}`, which is character-for-character the prototype's literal for the shipped catalogue."
  },
  "homeOpenBooks": "open",
  "@homeOpenBooks": {
    "description": "The carousel's second count's unit, and it agrees with `homeScrolls`. Transcribed from `redesign.html:930`'s `libCount` — see `homeScrolls` for why the pair exists.\n\n**Feminine plural in Arabic** (`مفتوحة`), because `دروج` is feminine and an Arabic adjective has to agree with its noun; `مفتوح` is the masculine form and reads as a separate word with no subject."
  },
  "homeVerses": "verses",
  "@homeVerses": {
    "description": "The unit in an open book card's caption. Transcribed: `redesign.html:966` — `verses:[\"verses\",\"آيات\"]`, composed at `:1313` as `${N(b.en.length)} ${tr('verses')}`.\n\n**Carried on open cards only.** `:1317` writes the category alone for a sealed one, because `SEALED` holds no verse array — see `LibraryBook.verseCount` for the null that distinguishes them."
  },
  "homeSealed": "sealed",
  "@homeSealed": {
